# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
config RUST_NOTIFIER
	bool "Rust notifier chains"
	depends on RUST
	default y
	help
	  Build notifier chain registration, traversal and the atomic,
	  blocking, raw, SRCU and die chain entry points from
	  kernel/notifier.rs in the original kernel/notifier.o slot. Native
	  companions keep the die chain storage, field/lock/RCU primitives,
	  tracepoint definitions, NOKPROBE and export metadata, and static
	  assertions of the public C signatures. Rust objects receive no
	  ftrace entry instrumentation, so notify_die keeps its notrace
	  behaviour. Turning this option off selects the unchanged C provider.
